lass=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with gasket, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the nuts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Nut</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Upper engine crankcase side) 0.8 ÷ 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2064597.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,1,0,"<p><a href=\"#/2752641\">1092G11</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2752826\">4450B04</a></p><p>Connect the lower coolant outlet hose to\nthe radiator and tighten the band.</p><p><a href=\"#/2752378\">0010T20</a>\n                                           .</p><p>Remove the car from the ramps.</p>"]]